## Candidate classification

### `xfmrover-over` — **New**
Last bound RT on **2026-03-09**; nothing for five months, then −701 over hr2–8 yesterday. Never binds DA at all (0 DA days in 104 weeks, 200 RT days). Sheet: seen 7×, last 2026-07-01, no physical_condition or outage_name recorded.

**Seasonal precedent: yes, but thin.** Same window last year it bound three days — 2025-07-23 (−270), 07-28 (−507), 07-29 (−155). Magnitudes an order of magnitude below its winter regime (Jan–Feb 2026 ran to −20,331 on 02-01). Its historical hourly shape is overnight-weighted (hr1–8 averaging −230 to −320) with an evening bump hr17–21, which is exactly the window it bound in yesterday.

Condition check works against it: zone-4 wind lift is +1.08 (binding prob 0.150 at top-95pct wind vs 0.072 baseline), and tomorrow zone 4 wind is at the 3rd percentile. The recurrence is not condition-supported. Treat as a low-conviction repeat of a small seasonal pattern.

### `lnrussett-sbrown` — **Momentum, but the driver is switching off**
Bound on 19 of the last 21 days, both sides, peaking 07-26/07-27 (RT −5171 / −4668). Sheet: 40 sightings, last 2026-07-31, "South OKGE", "binds high wind, no obvious outage nearby", wind=high, zones 3,4. Baseline binding rate 0.353 — this thing binds a third of all hours.

**But it is a high-wind constraint and tomorrow the wind is gone.** Zone-3 wind lift +1.04 (0.719 conditional vs 0.353 baseline); zone 3 on-peak wind tomorrow is at the **3rd** percentile, zone 4 at the 3rd. This qualifies as a **condition mismatch** despite the momentum, and DA is already showing it: −2012 on 07-31 collapsed to −291 on 08-01, and the six hours it kept were hr1–6 only. Expect a weak or absent day. Last year the same window carried it 20 days at up to −8663 RT, so August is its season — but the day-specific setup is against it.

### `lnnebrcty-sub3456` — **Condition mismatch on its dominant driver**
The only DA-side candidate, and DA-only by nature (0 RT days in 104 weeks, 219 DA days). Bound 12 of the last 21 days, heavy 07-27 → 07-30 (−2534, −3199, −3126, −1189), then −746 yesterday. Sheet: 23 sightings, last 2026-07-30, "S-N, Omaha", "384kv, low wind, 35% RT low wind, 25% high load", wind=low, zone 1. Linked to Cooper–Fairport, still out.

Zone-1 lifts: **load +2.43** (0.407 conditional vs 0.119 baseline) — the dominant driver — and **wind −0.92** (high wind drops it to 0.009, effectively kills it).

Tomorrow splits the two. **Load is the mismatch**: zone-1 load never exceeds the 48th percentile all day, well below the high-load state it needs. **Wind supports it** through the afternoon (22nd–45th percentile hours 10–17), then turns hostile late — zone-1 wind hits the 87th–97th percentile hours 22–24, which should relieve it in the evening. Your recorded condition (low wind) holds for the bidding window; the stronger statistical driver (high load) does not. Net: expect a materially weaker day than the 07-27→07-30 run, concentrated in the afternoon and gone by hr22. Last year this window gave it 11 days at −43 to −762 — the magnitude class it is in now.

### `lnmryvl_sj-midway5` — **Outage-driven, escalating, RT-only**
RT-only constraint (0 DA days ever). Bound 07-21 (−72), 07-31 (−110), 08-01 (−957) — escalating fast, and yesterday's was 8 hours, hr1–8. Sheet: seen once, 2026-06-10, no condition notes recorded. Linked to St Joe–Fairport 345 kV, out through **08-21**, so the cause persists through the bid date.

**No seasonal precedent** — it did not bind at all in the 2025-07-20 → 08-16 window; first observation is 2025-02-19, and its 2026 activity is Feb, May, Jun, and now. This is outage behaviour, not seasonal behaviour. Zone-4 wind lift is +5.51 (highest lift of any candidate: 0.080 vs 0.012 baseline) and tomorrow's zone-4 wind is at the 3rd percentile, so the statistical condition is against it — but that lift is measured across 104 weeks including long non-outage stretches, and the outage is doing the work right now. I'd weight the outage over the lift here. Caveat: everything about it is RT-only and yesterday's RT is a partial day.

